  "notes": "Fluent UI v9 styling of the Fluent Reader Electron app. A 680px white settings sheet sits centered on a warm gray #edebe9 backdrop, with a back arrow floating to its left. The tab strip mixes line icons and text, and the active tab has a blue 2-3px underline. Rows show colored square favicons (letter monograms). Selection is checkbox-based: the selected row turns grey and bold, and the 'Selected source' editor appears below the grid. Choosing several rows switches that editor to 'Selected multiple sources'. Delete is a red button that, on first click, becomes 'Confirm delete source?' in place. The primary button is blue #0f6cbd; secondary buttons are white with a #d1d1d1 outline. The Add button stays disabled grey until a URL is entered."
